The code statements that lead to the bug are:
```c
if (of_phy_is_fixed_link(pdev->dev.of_node)) {
    ret = of_phy_register_fixed_link(pdev->dev.of_node);
    if (ret < 0) {
        dev_err(&pdev->dev, "bad fixed-link spec\n");
        goto err_free_bus;
    }
}
```
Reason:
The code checks if the device tree node specifies a fixed-link PHY and attempts to register it. However, if the registration fails, it jumps to the `err_free_bus` label without deregistering the fixed-link PHY, leading to a memory leak since the resources associated with the fixed-link PHY are not released.

The code statements that fix the bug are:
```c
err_deregister_fixed_link:
if (of_phy_is_fixed_link(pdev->dev.of_node))
    of_phy_deregister_fixed_link(pdev->dev.of_node);
```
Reason:
These statements ensure that if an error occurs during the probe process or when the driver is removed, the fixed-link PHY is properly deregistered, thus preventing memory leaks by releasing the resources associated with it.

